# Backend Repo Context (Vero-Backend)

## Scope
This rules file applies to `/Users/sami/project/vero/Vero-Backend` and provides persistent backend context.

## Tech Stack & Architecture
- FastAPI backend with feature-based modules under `app/feature*/`.
- API routes live in `*_api.py`; business logic lives in `*_service.py`.
- PostgreSQL access via SQLAlchemy Core and `sqlalchemy.text()` queries.
- Multi-tenant behavior is workspace-driven and should remain explicit in request handling and data access.

## Required Backend Conventions
- No ORM model migration in feature code; keep raw SQL style consistent with repository patterns.
- Keep data access parameterized and tenant-aware.
- Prefer deterministic fixes and code-level guardrails over brittle one-off patches.
- Keep cache/version behavior explicit when LLM prompts/models or retrieval logic change.

## Testing & Quality Rules (Authoritative)
- Use existing test infrastructure only (`tests/unit`, `tests/integration`, `tests/quality`, `tests/live`).
- Do not create redundant/duplicate test files for existing features.
- Mock external APIs in unit/integration/quality tests; live tests are explicit and credit-burning.
- Preserve existing pytest marker usage and feature test organization.

## Important Programming Rules
- Preserve feature boundaries; avoid leaking cross-feature responsibilities.
- Keep API contracts stable and intentional for frontend consumers.
- Prefer clear, actionable errors over ambiguous failures.
- Avoid silent behavior changes that break existing client workflows.
